  "narrative": {
    "benchmark_md": "Peer set LOCKED in Batch 1 and immutable. Peer scores are category-level estimates from public signals \u2014 not full DMA assessments. PenFed added as aspirational outcome benchmark.",
    "issue_register_md": "Borrowed from DMA-RES-CCUIL-20260504-0001 \u00a75.1. Enriched with Layer 1 scoring impacts and connected cap analysis.",
    "per_pillar_md": {
      "P1": "Overall P1 Score: 2.502 | Peer Median: 3.12 | Gap: \u22120.62\nP1 profile: sharp contrast between people-facing capabilities (=2.77, =2.64) and strategy formalisation capabilities (=2.49, =2.33). CCU innovates through vendor selections rather than a published digital strategy document. ESG is active in practice but not formalised.",
      "P2": "Overall P2 Score: 2.558 | Peer Median: 3.47 | Gap: \u22120.91 | Largest Pillar by Weight (30%)\nP2 pattern: 'good tools, no intelligence layer.' Lumin Digital (=2.77) matches BCU's platform spec exactly \u2014 BCU overlays FSC+Agentforce to achieve 82% digital resolution [E-194]; CCU has Creatio+Talkdesk only. Creatio (=2.56) has hit its ceiling. is architecturally capped by <2.5.",
      "P3": "Overall P3 Score: 2.535 | Peer Median: 3.37 | Gap: \u22120.83\nP3 is CCU's most balanced pillar: genuine anchor strength in (RTP+FedNow + Zerto DR); structurally constrained (cross-capped by <2.5); well-grounded but not yet automated and.",
      "P4": "Overall P4 Score: 2.027 | Peer Median: 3.17 | Gap: \u22121.14\nP4 tells the sharpest story: Security (2.80) is an outlier strength \u2014 more sophisticated than most $4.3B credit unions. (Data, 1.73) and (AI, 1.73) are the two weakest categories across the entire four-pillar assessment. (Integration, 2.06) fires two connected caps. PATTERN-2 (AI Infrastructure Gap) and PATTERN-3 (Four-Merger Integration Deficit) define P4."
    },
